  ABSTAINED - no permitted action fits the evidence
  if wrong    : This abstention is wrong if someone produces evidence meeting an action's precondition — e.g. kube events or restart counts showing one of the four containers in CrashLoopBackOff or repeatedly restarting since 17:16:04, which would point at process state and justify restart_service on that specific service. It is also wrong if change history outside the 24-hour window shows a prior image tag or prior ConfigMap for one of these services, which would make rollback_image or revert_config eligible. Note separately: with Prometheus, Loki and Jaeger all unreachable from this vantage point [tr_e66eea973aa7, tr_8e06eccc4879, tr_bf905e3b47c4], the effect of ANY remediation taken now could not be observed through metrics, logs or traces — an unverifiable action is a second reason to hold.
