  root cause  : Not established. Every observability dispatch failed in the tooling transport path — Prometheus, Loki and Jaeger hostnames all failed DNS resolution from the querying environment, so no metric, log or trace signal was obtained for any of the four services. The only substantive evidence is the change log: nginx-web-server, compose-post-service, home-timeline-service and user-timeline-service were each stood up for the first time at 17:16:04–17:16:05 by platform-automation, with ConfigMap, Service and container created together and no prior revision of any of them in the 24-hour window. That establishes the whole stack is seven minutes old at onset — so whatever is failing has been failing since first start rather than regressing — but it does not identify which service is at fault or by what mechanism. nginx-web-server is named only as the edge where failure was observed, not as a demonstrated culprit.
  OPEN        : Which of the four services is actually failing — no trace, metric or log evidence implicates or exonerates any of them [tr_bf905e3b47c4].
  OPEN        : Did the containers created at 17:16:04 reach a healthy running state or fail at startup? This needs kube events or restart counts, since the log path is unusable [tr_415f12bc7d74].
  OPEN        : Is the DNS failure confined to the investigation tooling, or is cluster DNS degraded in a way that would also break service-to-service resolution inside social-network? The client-side judgement [tr_1ceb73156868] rests on the host being an observability endpoint, not on any test of in-cluster resolution.

